₦1,550 to ₦3,144.32 in 10 years semi-annually: i = (2.02859)^(1/20) − 1 = 0.036, nominal = 2 × 3.6% = "},{"text":"7.20%","bold":true},{"text":" (not 3.60%)."}]},{"text":[{"text":"Effective rates.","bold":true},{"text":" 16% quarterly: (1.04)^4 − 1 = 0.1699 = "},{"text":"16.99%","bold":true},{"text":". 24% monthly: (1.02)^12 − 1 = "},{"text":"26.824%","bold":true},{"text":". 10% continuously: e^0.1 − 1 = "},{"text":"10.52%","bold":true},{"text":". Comparing banks: 11.6% monthly gives 12.24%; 11.8% semi-annually 12.15%; 11.4% continuously 12.08%; 12% annually 12.00%. The "},{"text":"11.6% monthly","bold":true},{"text":" offer is best. For an effective 21% with quarterly compounding: 4[(1.21)^(1/4) − 1] = 4 × 0.04881 = "},{"text":"19.52%","bold":true},{"text":"."}]},{"text":[{"text":"Continuous.","bold":true},{"text":" ₦3,500 at 3.4% for 6 years: 3,500e^0.204 = "},{"text":"₦4,292.04","bold":true},{"text":". ₦500 at 8% for 9 years 3 months: 500e^(0.08 × 9.25) = 500e^0.74 = "},{"text":"₦1,047.97","bold":true},{"text":". ₦5,000 at 6% for 20 years: 5,000e^1.2 = "},{"text":"₦16,600.58","bold":true},{"text":". ₦250,000 at 9% for 5 years: 250,000e^0.45 = "},{"text":"₦392,078.05","bold":true},{"text":". ₦100,000 to ₦150,000 in 5 years: r = ln 1.5/5 = "},{"text":"8.11%","bold":true},{"text":". ₦2,000 at 10% to pass ₦2,100: t = ln 1.05/0.1 = 0.48790 year × 365 = 178.08, so "},{"text":"179 days","bold":true},{"text":". ₦1,000,000 for 3 years at 10%: continuous 1,349,858.81 − annual 1,331,000 = "},{"text":"₦18,859","bold":true},{"text":" more."}]}]}]},{"number":"6.4","title":"Present value, net present value and bonds","mustKnow":[{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"text":[{"text":"Discounting:","bold":true},{"text":" finding the present value of a sum due in the future (the reverse of compounding)."}]},{"text":[{"text":"Present value:","bold":true},{"text":" P = F(1 + i)^(−n) = F/(1 + i)^n. (1 + i)^(−n) is the "},{"text":"compound discount factor","bold":true},{"text":". Continuous: P = Fe^(−rt)."}]},{"text":[{"text":"Net present value (NPV)","bold":true},{"text":" = sum of present values of all future returns − initial cost."}],"blocks":[{"type":"list","ordered":true,"start":1,"items":[{"text":[{"text":"NPV > 0: returns are worth more than the cost in today's money; worth undertaking at that rate."}]},{"text":[{"text":"NPV < 0: reject. NPV = 0: the project earns exactly the discount rate."}]}]}]},{"text":[{"text":"Internal rate of return (IRR):","bold":true},{"text":" the rate at which NPV = 0."}]},{"text":[{"text":"Bond:","bold":true},{"text":" pays an annual return (coupon = coupon rate × face value) each year, plus the face value at maturity. Present value = PV of coupons + PV of face value, at the "},{"text":"current","bold":true},{"text":" interest rate. If the market rate is "},{"text":"above","bold":true},{"text":" the coupon rate, PV is "},{"text":"less than","bold":true},{"text":" face value; below it, PV is greater."}]}]}],"explainMore":[{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"text":[{"text":"₦2,500 due in 4 years at 10% quarterly: P = 2,500(1.025)^(−16) = 2,500/1.484506 = "},{"text":"₦1,684.06","bold":true},{"text":". ₦1,000 in 4 years at 10%: semi-annually 1,000/1.05^8 = "},{"text":"₦676.84","bold":true},{"text":"; continuously 1,000e^(−0.4) = "},{"text":"₦670.32","bold":true},{"text":". ₦1,000,000 in 5 years at 8%: 1,000,000/1.469328 = "},{"text":"₦680,583.20","bold":true},{"text":". ₦500,000 in 4 years at 6% continuously: 500,000e^(−0.24) = "},{"text":"₦393,313.93","bold":true},{"text":"."}]},{"text":[{"text":"Mr Bello's car:","bold":true},{"text":" ₦500,000 cash + PV of ₦300,000 in 3 years at 12% semi-annually = 500,000 + 300,000/1.06^6 = 500,000 + 211,488.16 = "},{"text":"₦711,488.16","bold":true},{"text":"."}]},{"text":[{"text":"Which offer?","bold":true},{"text":" ₦900,000 now or ₦1,200,000 in 3 years at 10%: PV = 1,200,000/1.331 = ₦901,577.76, which is more than ₦900,000, so the "},{"text":"later sum is better","bold":true},{"text":"."}]},{"text":[{"text":"NPV, worked.","bold":true},{"text":" Cost ₦2,000,000; ₦1.5 million at$study_guide$);
insert into private.study_guide_chunks (guide, ordinal, chunk) values ('study_guide_lag_acs213', 27, $study_guide$ year 5 and ₦1.25 million at year 6, at 4.5%:"}],"blocks":[{"type":"list","ordered":true,"start":1,"items":[{"text":[{"text":"1,500,000/1.045^5 = 1,500,000/1.246182 = 1,203,676.57"}]},{"text":[{"text":"1,250,000/1.045^6 = 1,250,000/1.302260 = 959,869.67"}]},{"text":[{"text":"NPV = 1,203,676.57 + 959,869.67 − 2,000,000 = "},{"text":"₦163,546.24","bold":true},{"text":"."}]}]}]},{"text":[{"text":"Cost ₦500,000, ₦200,000 a year for 3 years at 10%: 181,818.18 + 165,289.26 + 150,262.96 = 497,370.40; NPV = "},{"text":"−₦2,629.60","bold":true},{"text":" (reject). Cost ₦1,500,000; ₦600,000, ₦700,000, ₦500,000 at 8%: 555,555.56 + 600,137.17 + 396,916.12 = 1,552,608.85; NPV = "},{"text":"₦52,608.85","bold":true},{"text":"."}]},{"text":[{"text":"IRR:","bold":true},{"text":" cost ₦1,000,000, ₦1,210,000 after 2 years: (1 + r)^2 = 1.21, r = "},{"text":"10%","bold":true},{"text":"."}]},{"text":[{"text":"Bonds.","bold":true},{"text":" ₦6,000 bond, 6% return (₦360 a year), 3 years left, current rate 4%: 360/1.04 + 360/1.04^2 + 6,360/1.04^3 = 346.15 + 332.84 + 5,654.02 = "},{"text":"₦6,333.01","bold":true},{"text":" (above face value, because 4% < 6%). ₦10,000 bond, 8% coupon (₦800), 4 years, 10%: 800 × 3.169865 + 10,000/1.4641 = 2,535.89 + 6,830.13 = "},{"text":"₦9,366.03","bold":true},{"text":" (below face value). ₦20,000 at 9% (₦1,800), 3 years, 6%: 4,811.42 + 16,792.39 = "},{"text":"₦21,603.81","bold":true},{"text":"."}]}]}]},{"number":"6.5","title":"Annuities, sinking funds and perpetuities","mustKnow":[{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"text":[{"text":"Annuity:","bold":true},{"text":" a series of equal payments at regular intervals. "},{"text":"2 types:","bold":true}],"blocks":[{"type":"list","ordered":true,"start":1,"items":[{"text":[{"text":"Ordinary annuity:","bold":true},{"text":" each payment at the "},{"text":"end","bold":true},{"text":" of the period."}]},{"text":[{"text":"Annuity due:","bold":true},{"text":" each payment at the "},{"text":"beginning","bold":true},{"text":" of the period (also called an increasing annuity in savings questions)."}]}]}]},{"text":[{"text":"Future value of an ordinary annuity:","bold":true},{"text":" F = R[(1 + i)^n − 1]/i. R = payment per period, i = rate per period, n = number of payments. It is the sum of a geometric progression R + R(1 + i) + ... + R(1 + i)^(n−1)."}]},{"text":[{"text":"Future value of an annuity due:","bold":true},{"text":" F = R[(1 + i)^n − 1]/i × (1 + i) = R[(1 + i)^(n+1) − (1 + i)]/i. So "},{"text":"FV(due) = (1 + i) × FV(ordinary)","bold":true},{"text":"."}]},{"text":[{"text":"Sinking fund:","bold":true},{"text":" equal deposits to build a set sum A by a future date. "},{"text":"R = Ai/[(1 + i)^n − 1]","bold":true},{"text":"."}]},{"text":[{"text":"Perpetuity:","bold":true},{"text":" payments forever from interest alone, fund never used up. Fund = payment per period/rate per period. If payments are yearly but compounding is not, use the effective annual rate: fund = annual payment/[(1 + i)^m − 1]."}]},{"text":[{"text":"Total deposited = nR; interest earned = F − nR."}]}]}],"explainMore":[{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"text":[{"text":"Ordinary, worked.","bold":true},{"text":" ₦100 at the end of every quarter for 10 years at 8% quarterly: i = 0.02, n = 40. F = 100[(1.02)^40 − 1]/0.02 = 100 × 60.401983 = "},{"text":"₦6,040.20","bold":true},{"text":". Others: ₦1,000 every 6 months for 9 years at 10% (i = 0.05, n = 18): "},{"text":"₦28,132.38","bold":true},{"text":". ₦50,000 a year, 6 years at 10%: 50,000 × 7.7156 = "},{"text":"₦385,780.50","bold":true},{"text":". ₦10,000 monthly for 2 years at 12% (i = 0.01, n = 24): 10,000 × 26.973465 = "},{"text":"₦269,734.65","bold":true},{"text":"."}]},{"text":[{"text":"Annuity due, worked.","bold":true},{"text":" ₦50 on the first day of each month for 2 years at 6% monthly: i = 0.005, n = 24. Ordinary factor = (1.00